  "repo_truth": "The exact 48-path raw-byte subject is the complete bounded HCM-2.2 candidate-1.3 implementation after every Review 1 finding and Review 2 finding HCM-2.2-R2-001 were accepted and repaired test-first. Historical candidate 1.0, 1.1, and 1.2 admission is now version-exact and requires stored/derived identity equality while preserving valid history as safe nonmatches. The frozen lifecycle-result 1.0 and promotion-intent 1.2 schema documents remain unchanged. Native workspace, focused RED/GREEN, W/R/S recovery, Linux installed-runtime, package, schema, archive, handoff, link, scope, secret, formatting, Clippy, docs, and frozen-byte proofs pass. Independently establish correctness; this summary and all earlier verdicts are non-authoritative.",
  "allowed_scope": [
    "Remain read-only and replay all 48 manifest hashes, sorted order, and aggregate before review.",
    "Read AGENTS.md, selected handoff, exact-document decision, complete SPEC, implementation/review plan, current checklist, all three implementation proof files, Review 1/2 dispatches, rejected atomic-stage Review 3 dispatch, and every manifest path.",
    "Review the complete HCM-2.2 implementation for correctness, identity acyclicity, exact-byte authority, stable replay, evidence preservation, version-exact history, approval quorum, definition closure, atomicity, recovery, lifecycle, product cutover, tests, documentation truth, and bounded scope.",
    "Independently reproduce and audit HCM-2.2-R2-001 plus all three Review 1 findings and their test-first remediations.",
    "Attempt to falsify every required coherent rewrite, timestamp rewrite, wrong digest/length, semantic/raw crossing, forged/multiple candidate, zero/one/many discovery, malformed/historical/orphan/missing, unsafe store, stale-authority, W0-W15, R0-R9, and S0-S11 case.",
    "Return Critical, Required, Optional, and Nit findings first with exact file/line evidence, reproduction where possible, and smallest bounded remediation."
  ],
  "non_goals": [
    "No edits, staging, commits, handoff/ledger writes, branch changes, preservation-root mutation, or user task hops.",
    "No HCM-2.3, generic custom-kind intake, remaining artifact conversion, Resolution/Projection/Snapshot/posture-kernel, SDK/Tauri/Substrate/dock/publication work, or unrelated cleanup.",
    "Do not rely on proof summaries, Review 1/2 conclusions, rejected checkpoint behavior, parent conclusions, or success-asserting documentation as authority."
  ],
  "tasks": [
    "Invoke the ordered required skills and return BLOCKED on any subject path, hash, order, count, or aggregate mismatch.",
    "Admit the exact 48-path subject and read the full diff plus relevant surrounding code before commenting.",
    "Audit candidate-subject/result/final-candidate/approval/promotion/intent identity for cycles, implicit bindings, self-authentication, copied authority, or currentness gaps.",
    "Audit the complete frozen lifecycle-result 1.0 schema enforcement and independently authenticate semantic plus exact persisted result authority.",
    "Audit version-exact candidate 1.0/1.1/1.2 historical admission, stored/derived ID and filename equality, complete field semantics, safe-nonmatch preservation, malformed refusal, and candidate 1.3 reauthor/new-approval enforcement.",
    "Audit author-lock double inventory, zero/one/many/orphan/missing behavior, approval quorum derivation, exact resolved-definition projection, and fail-before-delta preservation.",
    "Audit promotion/recovery against semantic/exact result, create/amend basis, canonical/policy/lifecycle/observation/coverage/registry authority, and retained historical-head currentness.",
    "Audit every W0-W15, R0-R9, and S0-S11 boundary for unauthenticated mutation, evidence loss, partial authority, or unsupported completion.",
    "Audit compiler/CLI/runtime vectors/live smokes, frozen schemas, test-only hooks, package/platform behavior, control-pack truth, and HCM-2.3 exclusion.",
    "Return CLEAN only when no Critical, Required, Optional, or Nit finding remains; otherwise return CHANGES_REQUIRED or BLOCKED without repairing the subject."
  ],
